# Coarse-grid sweep (local-mode View C)

**What this is.** For a grid of resolutions (Mb), the collector
re-tiles every haplotype and measures the agreement between
popout's coarse call and FLARE's coarse call for each tile;
"diagonal fraction" is the share of tiles where the two
labels agree. Each faint grey line is one (cluster, sample,
haplotype, chrom); the bold green line is the per-resolution
median across all series.

**How to read this chart.** A diagonal fraction near 1.0 at small
resolutions (<= 1 Mb) means popout and FLARE largely agree at
high spatial resolution. If the green line *rises* with
resolution that means disagreements live below the smoothing
scale — coarsening the bins makes them cancel out. If the green
line is flat-and-low at every resolution the two tools disagree
fundamentally, not just locally.

